The [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue and one queued fix.
The exported logic shows two distinct causes. Split the work into a parser issue and a
booking-form hint issue. A queued fix is not evidence that either problem is resolved.

<Reassessment />

## Check the supplied classification

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Tenant locale comes from the tenant directory. Use `Intl.DateTimeFormat` to determine
the date order. For a day-first tenant, a `form` report through `booking-v3` belongs to
`hint`; other channels belong to `parser`. Browser locale and `meta.intakeTag` are intake
guesses. They do not establish the tenant's date order or the cause.

The parser reads month first. For example, a day-first date `07/04/2026` for 7 April
can become 4 July. The separate booking-v3 problem prints `MM/DD/YYYY` while its form
reader uses the tenant's day-first order. Each needs its own fix and its own ticket.

## Check the timeline

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Replace subject-only triage

The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) and [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)
were reviewed in June 2024. Their subject-only merge rule conflicts with the executable
examples below. Treat that rule as stale. Keep the accepted decision as history;
propose a new decision that replaces it before changing desk policy.

<DedupeExplorer />

Matching subjects can describe different causes. Different subjects can describe the
same cause. Compare the tenant, its locale, its booking form, the report channel and
the observed failure. Merge only when the cause matches. With a missing tenant or an
unclear symptom, keep the report separate until the desk has the missing evidence.

## Scope and limits

This page reclassifies the exported evidence. It does not change either booking path,
fix a product, or verify a production release. The counts describe the 4 October export.
The desk keeps working; reconcile later reports before treating these as current totals.

